<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Gurgum</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 BCE – 711 BCE (approx.) · capital Marqas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gurgum, a Neo-Hittite kingdom centred on Maraş, whose kings left Luwian inscriptions and lion sculptures before Assyria annexed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gurgum arose after the Hittite collapse in the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksu">Aksu</a> river around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahramanmaras">Marqas</a>, modern Kahramanmaraş, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. A local dynasty ruled it from the 10th century BCE or earlier.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings, several called Halparuntiya, left Luwian hieroglyphic inscriptions on stelae and lion statues recording their family line and building works. Gurgum joined alliances with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samal">Sam'al</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bit-agusi">Arpad</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and paid tribute to it as circumstances required.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>King Tarhulara was murdered by his son Mutallu. In 711 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> deposed Mutallu and annexed Gurgum as the province of Marqasi.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gurgum.jpg" alt="Gurgum" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Hans van Deukeren · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NeoHittiteStates.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 BCE – 711 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Marqas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Halparuntiya, Tarhulara, Mutallu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marqasi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-906&amp;focus=gurgum" aria-label="Gurgum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5602 825 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gurgum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5922 1081L6092 1134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5922 1081h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5922 1081h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-906&amp;focus=gurgum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

